Package: pve-cluster
Architecture: all
# libqb100 is listed manually: dh_shlibdeps is skipped for Architecture:all
# packages, but the bundled PVE/IPCC/IPCC.so links against libqb (SONAME 100).
Depends: libpve-common-perl,
         libqb100,
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${perl:Depends},
Description: @SUMMARY@
 @DESCRIPTION@
 This is a build-environment stub, not the real pve-cluster service: it
 only ships the Perl modules, without the pmxcfs daemon, corosync or
 pvecm. It exists so that pve-container's build-dep chain can be built
 from scratch in this repository without access to the official Proxmox
 apt repository.

Package: libpve-cluster-perl
Architecture: all
Depends: libpve-common-perl,
         librrds-perl,
         pve-cluster (= @FULL_VERSION_DEB@),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${perl:Depends},
Description: Proxmox VE cluster configuration library (build stub)
 Perl modules from the pve-cluster package (PVE::Corosync,
 PVE::DataCenterConfig, PVE::RRD, PVE::SSHInfo), shipped as
 Architecture:all so they can satisfy build dependencies in a
 from-scratch build without the real pve-cluster binary package.
